ll (0.2261 CER, 82.22% strict\n793\tcorrectness, and 69.53% both-output success), but\n794\tits launch CLI was not fully preserved; the causal\n795\teffect of the loss requires matched retraining, and\n796\tall rows are single checkpoints. Finally, input-only\n797\tconditioning retains 63.85% residual overlap versus 12.45% with FiLM. This diagnostic associates\n798\tlayer-wise conditioning with stronger suppression,\n799\tbut the checkpoints differ in training configuration\n800\tand do not form a controlled ablation.\n801\t\n802\t19.39\n803\t9.18\n804\t7.97\n805\t84.28\n806\t17.57\n807\t17.60\n808\t12.45\n809\t63.85\n810\t\n811\t7\n812\t\n813\t74.33\n814\t59.01\n815\t58.36\n816\t7.86\n817\t75.93\n818\t75.38\n819\t82.22\n820\t33.50\n821\t\n822\t6.28\n823\t31.82\n824\t33.68\n825\t7.86\n826\t6.50\n827\t7.02\n828\t5.33\n829\t2.64\n830\t\n831\t92.21\n832\t64.97\n833\t63.41\n834\t50.00\n835\t92.11\n836\t91.48\n837\t93.91\n838\t92.69\n839\t\n840\t58.51\n841\t30.74\n842\t28.77\n843\t0.00\n844\t59.89\n845\t60.40\n846\t69.53\n847\t12.36\n848\t\n849\tConclusion\n850\t\n851\tQ IANG DA turns audio-visual TSE into a paired\n852\tidentity test: the same jointly recorded mixture\n853\tmust yield A under A’s lip cue and B under B’s lip\n854\tcue. VOX B LINK 2-AVSE supplies 766 hours of\n855\tidentity-diverse aligned training data, while frozen\n856\tAV-HuBERT features, speaker margin training,\n857\tand layer-wise FiLM make the target cue explicit\n858\tthroughout the separator. The ablations show that\n859\tmatched training data and interferer suppression\n860\tmatter more than simply enlarging the GridNet\n861\tback end; the auxiliary speaker loss requires a controlled rerun before drawing a causal conclusion.\n862\tSpeaker margin, OSD-first strict identity rates, and\n863\tQwen3-ASR CER jointly test whether an extractor follows visual intent, suppresses overlap, and\n864\tpreserves the requested utterance.\n865\t\n866\t\fReferences\n867\tTriantafyllos Afouras, Joon Son Chung, an